            "detailed_description": "<h1>Steam Remote Play Together Ready!</h1><p><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/512160/extras/a35bb1c1760cfc7fa42d1dcb35c11ef0.avif?t=1783913575\" width=800 height=450 /></span><br>You can now play Volleying online with your friends through <strong>Steam Remote Play Together</strong>!<br>Learn More...</p><br><h1>Acerca do jogo</h1><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Pure Physics. Zero Softwares Deciding For You.</h2>Tired of sports games where pre-calculated animations decide the outcome? Volleying is fully physics-based. Your control, your timing, and the bouncing ball dictate the match. Every round is completely unique and beautifully chaotic.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Predictably Unpredictable Gameplay:</strong> Control your sphere, dominate the court, and make the ball touch the opponent’s ground. Sounds simple? Wait until the physics kick in.<br></li><li><strong>The 10-Second Exploding Ball Rule:</strong> No passive playing here! Once you touch the ball, you have exactly 10 seconds to send it back over the net, or it will explode, costing you the point.<br></li><li><strong>Dash Mechanics:</strong> Jump and trigger a quick dash in any direction (or upwards) to save impossible balls. Use it wisely— it takes 5 seconds to recharge!<br></li><li><strong>Arcade Mode Madness:</strong> Catch random items that spawn on the court to temporarily alter your size (or the ball's), creating hilarious and unexpected situations.<br></li><li><strong>In-Game Soundtrack Controls:</strong> Love the music? You can seamlessly skip and navigate between the soundtracks at any time during gameplay by simply pressing the square brackets ([ and ]).</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Play It Your Way</h2>Bring your friends over or use <strong>Steam Remote Play Together</strong> to experience the ultimate casual showdown. Supports 1v1, 1v2, 2v2, or a cooperative mode where you and a friend team up against the CPU.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Make It Yours: Custom Skins &amp; Courts</h2>Want to play with your own artwork? Volleying lets you fully customize player and court textures!<br>    <ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Right-click Volleying in your Steam Library &gt; Properties &gt; Installed Files &gt; Browse.<br>    </li><li>Open the &quot;conf&quot; directory to find the template (.png) files and quick instructions.<br>    </li><li>Fire up your favorite image editor, create your skins, and feel free to share your creations in our Steam Artwork community tab!</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A Note From the Developer</h2>Volleying is a true solo passion project built entirely from scratch without a commercial game engine. Developed natively on Linux using C++, custom OpenGL, and low-level libraries such as GLFW, Bullet Physics, OpenAL, and libzip, it stands as a tribute to raw code and the power of programming from the ground up. Windows was utilized strictly for cross-compiling and debugging.<br>Every visual and audio asset was crafted leveraging the vast ecosystem of professional open-source creative software—utilizing tools such as Blender, GIMP, Inkscape, Ardour, and Kdenlive across the pipeline.<br>If you appreciate independent, engine-free development and enjoy the game, leaving a quick review here on Steam helps a solo creator more than you know. Thank you for supporting the open-source spirit!",
            "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Pure Physics. Zero Softwares Deciding For You.</h2>Tired of sports games where pre-calculated animations decide the outcome? Volleying is fully physics-based. Your control, your timing, and the bouncing ball dictate the match. Every round is completely unique and beautifully chaotic.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Predictably Unpredictable Gameplay:</strong> Control your sphere, dominate the court, and make the ball touch the opponent’s ground. Sounds simple? Wait until the physics kick in.<br></li><li><strong>The 10-Second Exploding Ball Rule:</strong> No passive playing here! Once you touch the ball, you have exactly 10 seconds to send it back over the net, or it will explode, costing you the point.<br></li><li><strong>Dash Mechanics:</strong> Jump and trigger a quick dash in any direction (or upwards) to save impossible balls. Use it wisely— it takes 5 seconds to recharge!<br></li><li><strong>Arcade Mode Madness:</strong> Catch random items that spawn on the court to temporarily alter your size (or the ball's), creating hilarious and unexpected situations.<br></li><li><strong>In-Game Soundtrack Controls:</strong> Love the music? You can seamlessly skip and navigate between the soundtracks at any time during gameplay by simply pressing the square brackets ([ and ]).</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Play It Your Way</h2>Bring your friends over or use <strong>Steam Remote Play Together</strong> to experience the ultimate casual showdown. Supports 1v1, 1v2, 2v2, or a cooperative mode where you and a friend team up against the CPU.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Make It Yours: Custom Skins &amp; Courts</h2>Want to play with your own artwork? Volleying lets you fully customize player and court textures!<br>    <ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Right-click Volleying in your Steam Library &gt; Properties &gt; Installed Files &gt; Browse.<br>    </li><li>Open the &quot;conf&quot; directory to find the template (.png) files and quick instructions.<br>    </li><li>Fire up your favorite image editor, create your skins, and feel free to share your creations in our Steam Artwork community tab!</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A Note From the Developer</h2>Volleying is a true solo passion project built entirely from scratch without a commercial game engine. Developed natively on Linux using C++, custom OpenGL, and low-level libraries such as GLFW, Bullet Physics, OpenAL, and libzip, it stands as a tribute to raw code and the power of programming from the ground up. Windows was utilized strictly for cross-compiling and debugging.<br>Every visual and audio asset was crafted leveraging the vast ecosystem of professional open-source creative software—utilizing tools such as Blender, GIMP, Inkscape, Ardour, and Kdenlive across the pipeline.<br>If you appreciate independent, engine-free development and enjoy the game, leaving a quick review here on Steam helps a solo creator more than you know. Thank you for supporting the open-source spirit!",
            "short_description": "Dive into predictably unpredictable matches where physics reigns supreme! Master the wacky movement, use timely dashes, and trigger explosive game-changing items in arcade mode. Volleying delivers fast-paced, pure physics-based fun perfect for solo play or chaotic local/remote matches with friends.",
